\n243\t    - **WI-099** — mechanize the trace↔derive_gate rule-set sync promise with a\n244\t      meta test (M1 — closes the one found path to a silent gate/trace\n245\t      disagreement; cheap, high leverage).\n246\t    - **WI-100** — root-anchor `check.py`'s `docs/gate`/`docs/stack.ini` reads\n247\t      or fail loudly off-root (M2).\n248\t    - **WI-101** — state the Status-casing rule once + near-miss hint in the\n249\t      finding text (M3).\n250\t    - **WI-102** — gen_trajectory hygiene: one module-level `_esc` (now defined\n251\t      6×) + SVG node `<title>` labels (M4/L7; one regeneration, `--check` keeps\n252\t      it honest).\n253\t    - **WI-103** — PROCESS_OPTIONS byte budget + applies-when index table (M5;\n254\t      any doc *split* additionally needs an owner taste ruling).\n255\t    - **WI-105 — DONE 2026-07-13** — coverage plumbing hardening (M9/L1). Verified\n256\t      WI-104's pin is the primary remedy (clean 91.23%, 0 debris, stale\n257\t      `.coverage.*` self-heals); raised the meta coverage floor 80 → 85 as the\n258\t      regression sensor; declined the dedicated-child-dir rewrite. The record is\n259\t      the WI-105 row Deliverable + [log.md](log.md).\n260\t    - **WI-115** — status-currency hardening (owner-asked 2026-07-12): a\n261\t      warn-first `check_trajectory` finding when `docs/run-state` holds an\n262\t      end-state over an actionable queue (the observed agent-resume-parks-at-\n263\t      boot trap), plus the policy-flip status sweep as protocol (skills +\n264\t      reviewer charter). Spec: [specs/WI-115.md](specs/WI-115.md).\n265\t    - _(Not filed, deliberately: L5 commit-subject length — accept, or it needs\n266\t      a commit-msg check to be a backed rule; L6 template-cell manuals — an\n267\t      owner taste ruling on a deliberate design, medium churn to shipped\n268\t      templates; M8/L3 fold into WI-081/WI-080 as noted above.)_\n269\t- **Next action — the G3 backlog (branch `derived-gate-model`; `docs/next-wi` =\n270\t  WI-078).** Phase v2 is complete; the dev-toolchain pin (WI-104) and **the\n271\t  coverage-plumbing hardening (WI-105) both landed 2026-07-13** (see log.md); a\n272\t  resume session picks up WI-078 next (backlog below).\n273\t  1. **Derived-gate campaign — LANDED (this branch).** The design\n274\t     ([specs/derived-gate-model.md](specs/derived-gate-model.md)) is ratified and\n275\t     the whole 8-slice campaign has shipped: the `Draft` artifact state + trace\n276\t     exemption, SN section-as-state maturity, `scripts/derive_gate.py` (the gate\n277\t     computed from artifact states + cached to `docs/gate` with a `--check` rot\n278\t     guard), `check.py` consuming the derived gate (the `derived-gate` freshness\n279\t     step + pre-commit floor), the `[phase]-[g*]` archetype + phase-drop detector,\n280\t     the ratification workflow (`gate-advance` skill + `gate-policy`; ratification\n281\t     = a reviewed `Status`-change commit), the process-doc rewrite (PROCESS_OPTIONS\n282\t     \"Derived gate model\" + PROCESS.md §4/§7, **+785 B flagged**, baseline 59,638),\n283\t     and the migration + dogfood (the meta's own `docs/gate` is now the **derived**\n284\t     G3; `derive_gate --check` full-basis-passes). The **one open item** is the\n285\t     owner **G3 re-attestation** over the SR-049 spine cut (Needs \\<human> above).\n286\t     Phase v3+ now uses the derived gate: draft new SN/SR in the live spine, and\n287\t     the derived gate follows.\n288\t     *(The unattended-enablement step landed 2026-07-12 — the managed-routing\n289\t     consent layer + `single-ratify` gate authority; see the Unattended-layer\n290\t     bullet under Current State and its single-attest item in Needs \\<human>.)*\n291\t  2. **Phase v2 dev slices — BOTH DONE (v2 at G3).** The process-view slice\n292\t     closed 2026-07-12 (the Process tab, `process_panel()` per LLR-051, TC-051's\n293\t     7 nodes, SR-050 `Verified`, seam IF-052). The **tiered drill-down slice\n294\t     closed 2026-07-13**: `when_view()`/`_wi_phases()` + the shared\n295\t     `_campboxes`/`_wi_row`/`_wi_table` helpers give the When roadmap a\n296\t     phase ⊃ workstream ⊃ WI hierarchy (collapse at > 3 local members, campaign\n297\t     bottom tier, per-phase color accent, per-tier aggregated edges) and the\n298\t     How-SW view an expand-at-≤3/collapse-at->3 top view; LLR-052 `Implemented`,\n299\t     TC-052 `Verified` (9 pinned nodes), **SR-051 `Verified`**. The close\n300\t     regenerated the gate (v2 → G3) and passed `check.py --gate G3 --phase v1,v2`\n301\t     (14/14). Spec archived under `docs/archive/specs/` (path in the WI row's\n302\t     Deliverable). The v2 spine cut rides the owner single-ratify sitting above.\n303\t  3. **The rest of the backlog needs no new SR — proceed at G3** (`docs/next-wi`\n304\t     = WI-078): the dev-toolchain pin (WI-104) and the coverage-plumbing\n305\t     hardening (**WI-105 DONE 2026-07-13** — verified WI-104's pin closes the M9\n306\t     race/debris on one known toolchain, raised the meta coverage floor 80 → 85\n307\t     as the regression sensor; log.md) are both landed. Next: **WI-078**\n308\t     (dupes-gate + census — owner-ruled 2026-07-12, implementation only), then\n309\t     `main-decomposition` (WI-080 → WI-081), then WI-079 and the remaining\n310\t     deep-review-b queue (WI-099 the trace↔derive_gate sync test is the cheap\n311\t     high-leverage one; WI-100/101/102/115 the hygiene batch).\n312\t  Remaining owner item: the **push decision** above.\n313\t\n314\t## Scope\n315\t\n316\t- **Goal:** keep the kit **maintainable and trustworthy** — the\n317\t  `PROJECT-VISION:` tag opening [README.md](../README.md) is canonical.\n318\t- **Supported platforms:** Windows + POSIX; kit scripts stdlib-only on\n319\t  Python 3.8+.\n320\t- **Non-goals (self-application boundary):** no `run.*` product launchers (the\n321\t  kit's \"product\" is `project-trajectory/` + `tests/` — nothing to double-click\n322\t  launch); no scaffolded `docs/process.md` (the masters live in\n323\t  `project-trajectory/`). *(The SN-spine non-goal was **lifted by Thread 47** —\n324\t  the kit now traces itself; its registries live in `docs/requirements/` +\n325\t  `docs/test/`, distinct from the shipped `project-trajectory/registries/`\n326\t  templates.)*\n327\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5893326e-2caf-4290-a92f-184a7c73f0a4","uuid":"ae10be1d-a849-4f8a-bcc3-ff6b0351d378","timestamp":"2026-07-13T21:06:50.254Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\docs\\status.md","content":"# Meta-Repo Status — Blackboard\n\nThe **working surface** for developing the kit itself — the same `status.md`\npattern the kit scaffolds downstream, self-applied. This file is **forward-only**:\nonly what happens **next** lives here. The **WI registry** is\n[work-items.csv](requirements/work-items.csv) (each WI's backward-looking\n`Deliverable` records what shipped) and the **session/gate record** is\n[log.md](log.md). The kit's per-thread **design history** is archived at\n[archive/IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md](archive/IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md) — context, not a\nworking surface.\n\n- **Process (kit source):** [PROCESS.md](../project-trajectory/PROCESS.md) ·\n  [PROCESS_OPTIONS.md](../project-trajectory/PROCESS_OPTIONS.md) — this repo\n  has no scaffolded `docs/process.md`; the masters are the reference.\n- **Working rules:** [CLAUDE.md](../CLAUDE.md) + the `session-protocol` skill.\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n- **Bar:** `python -m pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` (the fast per-commit smoke\n  tier — ~47 s / 531 cases; full unfiltered suite ~66 s / 684 at\n  slice/campaign close) and\n  `python project-trajectory/scripts/check_docs.py --root . --stale` green\n  before every commit — this repo's standing gate. The kit's own\n  `SN→SR→LLR→TC` spine is self-adopted and the gate is **derived**\n  (`scripts/derive_gate.py`): with **phase v2 verified** (both v2 SRs\n  `Verified` 2026-07-13) the runnable `docs/gate` reads a uniform **G3** (basis\n  `per-phase=(default)=G3;v2=G3`); the full bar is\n  `check.py --gate G3 --phase v1,v2` (incl. the `derived-gate` freshness step),\n  and CI runs the derived gate on real data (the meta-repo dogfoods its own\n  trajectory + OKF + derived-gate layers).\n- **Plan state:** v1 spine at **G3** (re-attested 2026-07-12, all-mechanized;\n  the derived-gate campaign added **SR-049**, a mechanized Test SR, which\n  **rides a pending re-attestation** — Needs \\<human> above); **phase v2 now at\n  G3** — SR-050/SR-051 (the dashboard views, `Phase=v2`) ratified `Planned` by\n  the G1 LLM-gate review, decomposed to LLR-051/052 + TC-051/052 by the\n  `[v2]-[g2]` batch, then both **Verified by their dev slices** (SR-050 by the\n  Process tab 2026-07-12; **SR-051 by the tiered drill-down views 2026-07-13**,\n  `Test`, TC-052's 9 pinned pytest nodes). The whole v2 spine cut + the v2 → G3\n  advance **rides the owner's queued single-ratify sitting** (Needs \\<human>\n  below). Spine **SN=24\n  SR=51 LLR=52 TC=52, 0 orphans**, 52 declared interface seams, 5 declared components\n  (the meta's own How-SW top view is now 24 modules → 5 top-level components, 0\n  uncontained). The\n  dashboard is the root [`PROJECT_STATE.html`](../PROJECT_STATE.html). Session\n  history: [log.md](log.md).\n- **Unattended layer (enabled 2026-07-12; cross-provider + owner re-lineup same\n  day):** the kit's walk-away loop is wired for a managed, consent-explicit run —\n  `docs/gate-policy` = **`single-ratify`** (one human attest per phase batch;\n  register [gate-policy.md](gate-policy.md)), managed routing ON via\n  `docs/agents-enabled`: **6 pair rows / 2 families** in `docs/agents.csv` —\n  `ANTHROPIC` **Fable/Opus/Sonnet = strong/medium/quick** via the claude CLI\n  (Env pins `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=high`) and `OPENAI` GPT-5.6\n  **Sol/Terra/Luna = strong/medium/quick** via the opencode CLI.
